<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Samsung Corp to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Samsung Corp to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Samsung Corp will buy back 1.32 million common and 89,930 preferred shares of its own stock in the open market between February 1 and April 30 to boost its share prices, a company statement said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The buyback, representing two percent of the company's share capital, will be made by Samsung Securities at the previous day's closing price, the statement said.</p>
<p>Samsung Corp is a trading and construction unit of the</p>
<p>The company currently holds 194 common and one preferred shares of its own stock, the statement said.</p>
<p>Samsung Corp shares closed on Tuesday at 10,000 won.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
